WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.030
Who ever thought cheese could be so dangerous?

00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:06.817
In the high-stakes world of reality game shows,
anything can hurt!

00:00:07.505 --> 00:00:12.200
"The Amazing Race" has steadily pitted teams
of two in competitions around the globe for

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.750
over twenty years as one of CBS' most enduring
reality game shows.

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:22.130
In addition to embarking on the arduous journey,
contestants are tasked with unusual challenges

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.539
to help receive bonuses and other clues.

00:00:24.539 --> 00:00:28.920
One challenge involving watermelons explosively
backfired on a contestant.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.379
The Season 17 debut episode of "The Amazing
Race" had contestants travel across England

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:39.749
before using a slingshot to fire a watermelon
at a target to receive their next clue.

00:00:39.749 --> 00:00:44.179
After several missed attempts, contestant
Claire Champlin pulled back on the slingshot

00:00:44.179 --> 00:00:48.559
to fire the fruity projectile at the target,
only to have it flung right back into her

00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:50.120
face at full force.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:54.199
While the watermelon shattered on impact,
Claire was cleared by medical to continue

00:00:54.199 --> 00:00:56.890
the challenge, as encouraged by her teammate
Brook.

00:00:57.461 --> 00:01:02.920
Even on paper, the British competition series
"The Jump" sounds like a televised disaster

00:01:02.920 --> 00:01:04.280
in the making.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:08.430
Celebrity contestants are trained by mentors
to compete in various winter sports, including

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:09.720
a large ski jump.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:13.550
This potentially perilous premise was put
to the test during the show's third season

00:01:13.550 --> 00:01:18.300
in 2016, which featured a stunning number
of painful injuries that resulted in several

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.330
contestants withdrawing prematurely throughout
the season.

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.600
The withdrawals began early on, with contestant
Tina Hobley leaving the show after dislocating

00:01:26.600 --> 00:01:29.140
her elbow while training for the ski jump.

00:01:29.140 --> 00:01:32.920
She was followed by Rebecca Adlington, who
left after dislocating her shoulder while

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.670
training for an air jump.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:38.890
These events were followed by incidents occurring
to contestants Beth Tweddle, who suffered

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:43.980
a spinal injury; Mark-Francis Vandelli, who
broke one of his ankles; and Linford Christie,

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.920
who endured a hamstring injury.

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:50.050
Despite all the accidents, "The Jump" returned
for one additional season the following year,

00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:52.559
which saw its own set of contestant injuries.

00:01:52.971 --> 00:01:58.430
While "Dancing on Ice" is also a British competition
series featuring celebrity contestants and

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:01.760
winter sports, it has a much less hazardous
premise than "The Jump."

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:06.660
"Dancing on Ice" pairs contestants with figure
skating mentors, and the duos carry out elaborate

00:02:06.660 --> 00:02:10.929
routines each episode as they are steadily
eliminated based on the judges' scores.

00:02:10.929 --> 00:02:15.069
British actor Jennifer Ellison was paired
with figure skating mentor Daniel Whiston

00:02:15.069 --> 00:02:18.400
for the seventh season before a bloody incident
occurred.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.069
While performing a routine set to Peggy Lee's
"Fever," the actor accidentally kicked herself

00:02:23.069 --> 00:02:25.000
in the back of the head with her ice skate's
blade.

00:02:25.000 --> 00:02:30.668
"Well, um, we can see that, uh, Jen has actually
hurt her head."

00:02:30.668 --> 00:02:35.519
Though Ellison admirably managed to finish
her set despite bleeding profusely from her

00:02:35.519 --> 00:02:39.896
scalp, the duo were eventually eliminated
by the season's penultimate episode.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.829
There is something about British reality competition
shows putting their celebrity contestants

00:02:44.829 --> 00:02:46.310
in uncomfortable positions.

00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.980
This is especially true for "I'm a Celebrity...

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:49.980
Get Me Out of Here."

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:55.000
The series' tenth season in 2010 put its cast
in the untamed Australian wilderness, where

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:59.349
the contestants underwent challenges as they
endured the rigors of the jungle together.

00:02:59.349 --> 00:03:04.629
This resulted in contestants Shaun Ryder and
Lembit Opik having their own harrowing experiences

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:07.110
at the fangs of the local wildlife.

00:03:07.110 --> 00:03:11.510
One of the season's challenges had the contestants
forage through a set of boxes in search of

00:03:11.510 --> 00:03:15.370
a key, with several containing rats and one
housing a python.

00:03:15.370 --> 00:03:19.840
Both Ryder and Opik were bitten by the python
and required immediate medical attention.

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:24.349
Fortunately for the Happy Mondays frontman,
Ryder would eventually end his reality television

00:03:24.349 --> 00:03:28.719
stint as the season's runner-up, almost making
the gnarly snake bite worth the trouble.

00:03:29.241 --> 00:03:33.769
Like its American counterpart, the British
competition series "Total Wipeout" has its

00:03:33.769 --> 00:03:38.230
contestants traverse tricky obstacle courses,
often resulting in them plunging into the

00:03:38.230 --> 00:03:39.719
water or mud below.

00:03:39.719 --> 00:03:44.779
In addition to its full seasons, the program
aired special episodes with celebrity contestants.

00:03:44.779 --> 00:03:51.079
In 2011, comedian Dom Joly tried his hand
at the competition only to walk away … well,

00:03:51.079 --> 00:03:52.239
not really walk at all.

00:03:52.239 --> 00:03:56.730
While navigating through the special's big
ball obstacle course in Argentina, Joly broke

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.189
several bones in his foot.

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:01.980
The painful experience left him in recovery
for three months, though he claimed to The

00:04:01.980 --> 00:04:05.368
Mirror that his children were excited about
their father appearing on the show.

00:04:05.368 --> 00:04:10.469
The incident didn't put Joly off from future
reality television appearances, however; he

00:04:10.469 --> 00:04:14.799
appeared as a contestant during the 2016 season
of "Celebrity Island with Bear Grylls."

00:04:15.248 --> 00:04:19.670
The teams competing in "The Amazing Race"
come from a variety of backgrounds, be it

00:04:19.670 --> 00:04:22.160
co-workers, friends, couples, or families.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:26.520
These bonds are tested as the duos endure
some of the strangest, most grueling challenges

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.970
around the world to determine which team is
eliminated each week.

00:04:29.970 --> 00:04:36.230
"The Amazing Race" Season 14 featured one
father-son team who suffered a notably painful experience.

00:04:36.230 --> 00:04:40.910
In a nod to Switzerland — the season premiere's
opening location — the teams were tasked

00:04:40.910 --> 00:04:45.580
with carrying four 50-pound cheese wheels
down a hill using a fragile backpack.

00:04:45.580 --> 00:04:50.320
Among the participating teams was father-son
duo Mel and Mike White, who quickly discovered

00:04:50.320 --> 00:04:52.100
they bit off more than they could chew.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:56.720
Mel severely pulled his groin during the challenge
and was forced to gingerly transport the cheese

00:04:56.720 --> 00:05:00.670
by inching along on his butt with the hefty
dairy product in his lap.

00:05:00.670 --> 00:05:04.860
The team would eventually be eliminated in
the sixth episode, but they returned for the

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:07.130
18th season of "The Amazing Race."

00:05:07.266 --> 00:05:12.710
For "Survivor" Season 37, the long-running
reality competition show decided to pit perceived

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:18.801
underdogs against overachieving alpha types
in Fiji, subtitling the season "David vs. Goliath."

00:05:18.801 --> 00:05:23.580
The very first contestant to be eliminated
was Pat Cusack — one of the designated underdogs

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.740
— who left the show three days into filming.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:30.460
However, in contrast to his fellow contestants,
Pat wasn't voted off the island but instead

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:33.440
departed after suffering a severe spinal injury.

00:05:33.440 --> 00:05:35.560
He had to be airlifted from the show.

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:39.710
While the contestants were returning to the
island by boat, the ship was hit hard by a

00:05:39.710 --> 00:05:41.900
wave, resulting in Pat hurting his back.

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:46.020
His injury was later diagnosed as spinal compression
deterioration.

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:49.480
Pat's injury wasn't filmed, but the immediate
aftermath was.

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:53.960
Viewers witnessed him experiencing intense
pain as he was immobilized and struggling

00:05:53.960 --> 00:05:55.250
to maintain his composure.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:59.880
Though Pat recovered back home after being
medically evacuated, his early departure made

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:03.440
"Survivor" Season 37 begin on a decidedly
painful note.

00:06:03.981 --> 00:06:08.500
Of all the contestants on "The Amazing Race,"
some of the most unflappable are the married

00:06:08.500 --> 00:06:12.320
couple Gretchen and Meredith Smith, both of
whom appeared in Season 7.

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:16.340
The Smiths held the distinction of being the
oldest couple to make it to the final tour

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:20.750
on "The Amazing Race" to date, progressing
due to their tight teamwork and stoic resilience.

00:06:20.750 --> 00:06:25.010
And the most visible testament to the couple's
endurance and good humor about themselves

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:28.090
occurred when Gretchen experienced a particularly
bloody injury.

00:06:28.090 --> 00:06:31.950
As Gretchen and Meredith went on a spelunking
challenge to search for a clue, the former

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:34.930
slipped and cut her face badly in the darkened
cave.

00:06:34.930 --> 00:06:38.750
By the time the medics arrived on the scene,
her face was covered with blood.

00:06:38.750 --> 00:06:42.830
Even following a pretty gnarly accident, Gretchen
was in good spirits, joking,

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:47.164
"I've been wanting a facelift for a long time."

00:06:47.164 --> 00:06:51.420
While she and Meredith may not have won the
race, Gretchen's good-natured reaction to

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:55.348
her injury underscores why the couple was
so memorable compared to their competitors.

00:06:55.741 --> 00:07:00.700
The high-stakes world of competitive cheerleading
is explored in the Netflix original reality

00:07:00.700 --> 00:07:06.851
series "Cheer," with the first season following
the Navarro College Bulldogs on the national stage.

00:07:06.851 --> 00:07:11.020
Traveling from their home campus in Texas
to the National Cheerleading Championship

00:07:11.020 --> 00:07:15.930
in Daytona, Florida, the Bulldogs pulled out
all the stops in their bid to win the competition.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:20.230
But for all the practice that the cheerleaders
underwent to emerge triumphant, one nasty

00:07:20.230 --> 00:07:23.860
accident on the mat sidelined a prominent
member of the team.

00:07:23.860 --> 00:07:27.910
During the Bulldogs' national championship
performance, their teammate Austin Bayles

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:32.100
hurt his ankle, forcing the rest of the team
to pause their showcase and scramble to find

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.100
a replacement.

00:07:33.100 --> 00:07:37.580
The injury came after Austin performed a series
of back handsprings, coming down painfully

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:41.380
on his left ankle and forcing him to have
to watch the rest of the team perform from

00:07:41.380 --> 00:07:42.610
the sidelines.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:47.360
Fortunately, the Bulldogs proceeded to win
the 2019 championship title without Austin,

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:50.820
and he wound up transferring to Texas Tech
University the following year.

00:07:51.305 --> 00:07:56.310
Season 12 of "Survivor" took place in Panama,
as four tribes competed against each other

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:59.680
on the Pearl Islands to crown the season's
sole survivor.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:04.310
The winner was Aras Baskauskas, who was voted
sole survivor by his fellow contestants at

00:08:04.310 --> 00:08:05.310
the end of the season.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.420
But Aras' final day was not a complete triumph.

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:12.480
On the last day of filming, he suffered a
gruesome injury that resulted in him receiving

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:15.450
stitches before leaving the islands for good.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:20.840
While celebrating making it to the final day,
Aras and his fellow contestant Danielle DiLorenzo

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:23.930
drank a bottle of champagne together on some
rocks.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:28.360
While drinking, Aras slipped and fell, dropping
the bottle, which shattered below him before

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.610
he fell on top of the broken glass.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.560
He received seven stitches from the attending
medics on the spot after cutting up his hand

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:38.275
and was back before triumphing over Danielle
as the season champion.

00:08:38.275 --> 00:08:43.378
"Despite the fact that I made it 39 days,
I feel like my ego has been crushed."

00:08:43.514 --> 00:08:48.330
Not all game show fails are physically painful
in nature; the embarrassment of broadcasting

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:52.360
one's ignorance to the world is certainly
excruciating in its own right.

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:57.279
The public humiliation is palpable in a 2022
episode of "Wheel of Fortune," with all three

00:08:57.279 --> 00:09:01.580
contestants failing to solve a relatively
simple puzzle — even with virtually all

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.140
the letters completed.

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:07.870
And immediately after the episode aired, social
media was in a frenzy, lambasting the show's

00:09:07.870 --> 00:09:10.750
contestants' inability to figure out the puzzle.

00:09:10.750 --> 00:09:15.480
Trying to solve for the five-word phrase "another
feather in your cap," the three contestants

00:09:15.480 --> 00:09:20.700
respond with everything from "another feather
in your hat" to "another feather in your map."

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:25.210
Ultimately, the puzzle was solved, though
it took eight rounds and ten attempts before

00:09:25.210 --> 00:09:27.800
the correct answer was finally delivered.

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:32.330
Host Pat Sajak would later defend the contestants'
struggle, remarking that the experience in

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:35.630
solving a puzzle is "different in the studio"
setting.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:39.772
"How big is Really Really Big Man's kitchen?"

00:09:39.772 --> 00:09:42.317
"Eh, really really?"

00:09:42.997 --> 00:09:48.200
Of all the dating reality shows on television,
"The Bachelor" is something of a gold standard

00:09:48.200 --> 00:09:52.130
for the genre, as contestants vie for the
affection of its eligible lead.

00:09:52.130 --> 00:09:55.300
This results in all manner of heartbreak and
humiliation.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:09:59.800
The most painfully awkward and heartbreaking
incident on "The Bachelor" to date occurred

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:05.668
after a winner was presumably selected, leading
to a publicly messy breakup after the season concluded.

00:10:05.668 --> 00:10:10.480
"The Bachelor" Season 22 unfolded much like
any of the previous seasons, with the cutthroat

00:10:10.480 --> 00:10:16.050
competition and dangerous liaisons culminating
in Arie Luyendyk proposing to Becca Kufrin

00:10:16.050 --> 00:10:17.190
in the season finale.

00:10:17.190 --> 00:10:21.920
Arie quickly recognized that he had made a
mistake, however, appearing in a follow-up

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:27.140
television climax to break up with Becca and
embark on a romance with the season's runner-up

00:10:27.140 --> 00:10:28.650
Lauren Burnham instead.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:32.950
"Bachelor" fans denounced Arie for the public
switch after the season finale.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:37.710
The idea of using a whole episode broadcast
after the intended finale makes for one of

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:40.840
the most painfully embarrassing breakups in
television history.

